  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 4,\n  \"section_title\": \"Advanced Grammar and Structures (C1-C2)\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"C1-C2\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 31,\n      \"question\": \"It was the company's decision to lay off employees that led to the strike. Which of the following sentences best conveys the same idea using a cleft sentence?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The company's decision, it was, to lay off employees that led to the strike.\", \"Laying off employees, which was the company's decision, led to the strike.\", \"It was the decision to lay off employees that was made by the company and led to the strike.\", \"The company decided to lay off employees, which is what led to the strike.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"The company's decision, it was, to lay off employees that led to the strike.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 32,\n      \"question\": \"By the time I arrived at the party, most of the guests had already left. Which of the following sentences correctly uses the past perfect tense?\",\n      \"options\": [\"I had eaten before arriving at the party.\", \"Most of the guests had already left by the time I arrived.\", \"The food was still being served when I arrived.\", \"I had been waiting for over an hour when most of the guests left.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Most of the guests had already left by the time I arrived.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 33,\n      \"question\": \"Unless you learn to manage your time effectively, you will struggle to meet deadlines. Which of the following sentences correctly uses the third conditional?\",\n      \"options\": [\"If you learned to manage your time effectively, you would not struggle to meet deadlines.\", \"You had managed your time effectively if you hadn't struggled to meet deadlines.\", \"Unless you learn to manage your time effectively, you will struggle to meet deadlines.\", \"Had you managed your time effectively, you wouldn't have struggled to meet deadlines.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"If you learned to manage your time effectively, you would not struggle to meet deadlines.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 34,\n      \"question\": \"It is essential that the manager be present at the meeting. Which of the following sentences correctly uses the subjunctive mood?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The manager must be present at the meeting.\", \"It is necessary for the manager to be present at the meeting.\", \"That the manager be present at the meeting is crucial.\", \"The manager being present at the meeting would be ideal.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"That the manager be present at the meeting is crucial.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 35,\n      \"question\": \"What I said was not meant to offend anyone. Which of the following sentences correctly uses an ellipsis?\",\n      \"options\": [\"...or so I thought.\", \"I didn't mean to offend anyone, that's for sure.\", \"It wasn't my intention to cause any offense.\", \"What I said, and I'm sorry for it, was not meant to offend anyone.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"What I said, and I'm sorry for it, was not meant to offend anyone.\"\n  ]\n}",
